/E (Do not rush to have it all figured out, instead pay attention to what moves you, what troubles you enough to want to fix it, and what you find yourself returning to even when no one is watching or applauding. That quiet pull is often purpose, whispering. Do not be afraid of failure; it is often the classroom where resilience is built and greatness is refined. Invest in your character as diligently as you invest in your knowledge. Your greatest asset will never be your title, your qualifications, or your accomplishments alone, it will be your character. It is what sustains influence long after the applause has faded and is the foundation upon which lasting leadership is built.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
